<?xml version="1.0"?>
<robot xmlns:xacro="http://ros.org/wiki/xacro">
  <!-- PositionJointInterface, deliberately. THE GRIP COMES FROM fmax, NOT FROM THE INTERFACE.
       Read this before "fixing" it to EffortJointInterface.

       gazebo_ros_control drives a position-mode joint with SetPosition(), but it first calls
           joint->SetParam("fmax", 0, <URDF effort limit>)
       and that fmax bounds the force the joint may use to reach its target. With the stock
       effort="1000" the joint has effectively unlimited authority and simply bulldozes the
       fingers through whatever is between them. Measured on the 40 mm landmine detonator:
       finger_joint reached its commanded 0.556 exactly (a 40 mm block should have stalled it
       near 0.44), Gazebo's contact manager saw NOTHING, gazebo_grasp_fix (which attaches only
       on OPPOSING CONTACT FORCES) never fired once, and the mine never moved at all.

       So the fix is to BOUND the effort, not to change the interface: finger_joint's limit is
       now effort="20" (see robotiq_140_gripper.urdf.xacro), letting the joint stall on the
       object so real contact forces develop.

       Why not EffortJointInterface, the textbook answer? Because it forces a control_toolbox
       PID into the loop (effort_controllers/JointTrajectoryController requires `gains:`), and
       on THIS Noetic build any control_toolbox PID instantiated inside gzserver aborts it with
       std::bad_array_new_length. Bisected repeatedly: PID present => gzserver dies at startup
       every time; PID absent => starts every time. The same applies to
       /gazebo_ros_control/pid_gains/* and to the mimic plugin's <hasPID/> mode. Until that is
       diagnosed, PID-based force control is not available in this environment. -->
  <xacro:macro name="robotiq_arg2f_transmission" params="prefix">
    <transmission name="${prefix}finger_joint_trans">
      <type>transmission_interface/SimpleTransmission</type>
      <joint name="${prefix}finger_joint">
        <hardwareInterface>PositionJointInterface</hardwareInterface>
      </joint>
      <actuator name="${prefix}finger_joint_motor">
        <mechanicalReduction>1</mechanicalReduction>
      </actuator>
    </transmission>
  </xacro:macro>
</robot>
